error[NK1202]: `n > 0` is a claim about data from outside the program.
  --> tests/an_inferred_whole_let_without_a_guard.nika:8:5
   |
 8 |     assert(n > 0)
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: `n` comes from outside the program, so nothing the compiler can see says what it holds.
   = note: That it is wrong is a case the program has to handle, not a defect an `assert` catches.
   = help: Check it where it arrives, with a guard the program handles: `throw BadInput(n) if !(n > 0)`, or `return … if !(n > 0)`. After that line, this `assert` is proved.
